     * For each j, if the digit s[j] is non-zero, it determines the divisor k = value(s[j]).
     * Then, it checks all substrings s[i..j] (for 0 <= i <= j) for divisibility by k.
     * To do this efficiently in O(N) time, we use prefix properties and frequency maps/arrays.
     *
     * For k = 1, 2, 5: The divisibility condition is always met. Add j+1 to the count.
     * For k = 3, 6, 9: Divisibility depends on the sum of digits modulo 3 or 9. We use prefix sums S[j] = sum(s[0..j]) and frequency maps.
     *      Condition Sum[i..j] % m == 0 is equivalent to S[j] % m == S[i-1] % m (where m=3 or 9).
     *      The count of valid i's is the frequency of S[j] % m among previous prefix sums S[-1]..S[j-1].
     * For k = 4, 8: Divisibility depends on the last few digits. Specific rules are applied based on s[j], s[j-1], s[j-2].
     * For k = 7: Divisibility rule is complex. We use a transformation: N(i, j) % 7 == 0 is equivalent to R[j] % 7 == R[i-1] % 7,
     *      where R[x] = P[x] * (10^{-1})^{x+1} mod 7. P[x] is the value of prefix s[0..x]. 10^{-1} mod 7 is 5.
     *      We maintain frequencies of R values modulo 7.
     *
     * All checks and updates are done in O(1) time per index j, leading to O(N) total time complexity.
     * Space complexity is O(1) because the frequency arrays have constant sizes (3, 9, 7).
     */
    long long countSubstrings(string s) {
        long long ans = 0; // Use long long for the answer as it can exceed 32-bit integer limit.
        int n = s.length();

        // Frequency arrays to store counts of prefix properties modulo 3, 9, and 7 (for R value).
        // The index represents the remainder/value, and the value at that index is the count of prefixes having that property.
        vector<long long> freq3(3, 0); 
        vector<long long> freq9(9, 0); 
        vector<long long> freq7(7, 0); 

        // Initialize counts for the empty prefix (considered index -1).
        // Empty prefix sum is 0. Its corresponding R value R[-1] is also 0.
        freq3[0] = 1;
        freq9[0] = 1;
        freq7[0] = 1; 

        int S3 = 0; // Current prefix sum modulo 3, S[j] = Sum(s[0..j]) mod 3
        int S9 = 0; // Current prefix sum modulo 9, S[j] = Sum(s[0..j]) mod 9
        int P7 = 0; // Current prefix value P[j] = Value(s[0..j]) mod 7

        // current_pow5 stores 5^(idx+1) mod 7. It's needed for calculating R[idx].
        // Starts at 5^0=1 (for state before index 0). Updated inside loop before use for index j.
        long long current_pow5 = 1; 

        // Iterate through the string using index j as the end position of substrings.
        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {
            int v_j = s[j] - '0'; // Get the numeric value of the current digit s[j].

            // Update prefix properties based on the current digit v_j.
